<H1>Medium data</H1>
Search for medium no. = [519].
<HR>
Unless otherwise stated, sterilize media by autoclaving at 121&#176;C for 15 min.
<HR>
<P><B><FONT SIZE=3>519&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;SYNTROPHOMONAS MEDIUM (for Syntrophospora cellicola 19J-3)</FONT></B></P>
<I>Solution A:</I> <br>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Mineral solution (see below)                           </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;50.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> FeCl<sub>2</sub> solution (see Medium No. <a href="/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=187">187</a>)                 </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;1.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Trace element solution (see Medium No. <a href="/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=187">187</a>)           </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;1.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Rumen fluid, clarified (see Medium No. <a href="/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=266">266</a>)          </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;50.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Trypticase peptone (BD-BBL)                                </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;1.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Vitamin solution (see below)                            </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;5.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Butyric acid                                            </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;1.7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Na<sub>2</sub>SO<sub>4</sub>                                            </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;2.8&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Resazurin                                               </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;1.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> mg  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Distilled water                                       </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;795.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Mix components, adjust pH to 7.2, bring to a boil for a few seconds and cool down under a stream of a N<sub>2</sub>-CO<sub>2</sub> (80:20) gas mixture.  Distribute Solution A into culture vessels (e.g., 9 ml per tube) under the same gas mixture, seal with butyl rubber stoppers and autoclave.  <br>
To complete the medium, add 0.1 volume of 3.5% NaHCO<sub>3</sub> solution [filter-sterilized and stored under a N<sub>2</sub>-CO<sub>2</sub> (80:20) gas mixture] and reduce the medium with 0.3 g/L (final) L-cysteine&#183;HCl&#183;H<sub>2</sub>O and 0.3 g/L (final) Na<sub>2</sub>S&#183;9H<sub>2</sub>O (autoclave and store 3% stock solutions under a N<sub>2</sub> atmosphere).  <br>
<I>Mineral solution:</I> <br>
